('gobustan + old city tour',NULL,'Hotel','Hotel','41',41,'PrivateTransfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Gobustan National Park Museum followed by Gobustan Petroglyph Rock Art Cultural Landscape  Rock paintings of Gobustan were first discovered in 1939   by archaeologist I. Jafarzade. On this territory there are   many traces of primitive inhabitance of people belong to   the period of the Paleolithic and Mesolithic. Rock   engravings of Gobustan cover a long historical period   nearly 15,000 years. In the Gobustan can be found rock   paintings created in the primitive epoch and up to the   \\Middle Ages, nowadays there are about 6,000 drawings.   The territory of Gobustan had favorable living conditions   in the Mesolithic, Neolithic and Bronze Age and was   inhabited by hunters and fishermen. Petroglyphs of the   Gobustan museum included to the UNESCO World Heritage List. + Old City tour starts from Shamakhi Gates followed by Old city below places (Photo stop)  -Shamakhi Gates  -Sculptures of Azim Azimzadeh’s  -Caravanserai of Bukhara  -Caravanserai of Multani  -Maiden’s Tower  -Bazar Square  -Miniature Books’ Museum  -Shirvanshahs’ Palace',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',41.0),
